The [[anime]] television series is produced by [[Bones Film]] and directed by Fumihiko Suganuma, with [[Hiroshi Seko]] handling series composition and episode screenplays, Satoshi Ishino as [[chief animation director]] and character designer, and [[Taku Iwasaki]] as music composer. The series aired from July 6 to December 22, 2025, on the [[Agaru Anime]] programming block on all [[Japan News Network|JNN]] affiliates, including [[Chubu-Nippon Broadcasting|CBC]] and [[TBS Television (Japan)|TBS]], and ran for two consecutive [[Television in Japan#Programs|cours]].<ref>{{Cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|date=June 12, 2024|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-06-12/kei-urana-gachiakuta-manga-gets-2025-tv-anime-by-bones/.211875|title=Kei Urana's ''Gachiakuta'' Manga Gets 2025 TV Anime by Bones|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240613033135/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-06-12/kei-urana-gachiakuta-manga-gets-2025-tv-anime-by-bones/.211875|archive-date=June 13, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=June 13, 2024}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/608456|script-title=ja:アニメ「ガチアクタ」ルドの決意の表情捉えたビジュアル公開、セリフちりばめたPVも|website=[[Comic Natalie]]|language=ja|publisher=Natasha, Inc|date=January 21, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250121120807/https://natalie.mu/comic/news/608456|archive-date=January 21, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=January 23, 2025}}</ref><ref name="Cast">{{Cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|date=March 13, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-03-13/gachiakuta-tv-anime-teaser-reveals-cast-more-staff-july-debut-crunchyroll-streaming/.222341|title=''Gachiakuta'' TV Anime's Teaser Reveals Cast, More Staff, July Debut, Crunchyroll Streaming (Updated)|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315193900/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-03-13/gachiakuta-tv-anime-teaser-reveals-cast-more-staff-july-debut-crunchyroll-streaming/.222341|archive-date=March 15, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=March 14, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|last=Tai|first=Anita|date=July 6, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-07-06/gachiakuta-anime-to-run-for-half-year-without-breaks/.226387|title=''Gachiakuta'' Anime to Run for Half-Year Without Breaks|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250706235714/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-07-06/gachiakuta-anime-to-run-for-half-year-without-breaks/.226387|archive-date=July 6, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=July 6, 2025}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|date=June 6, 2025|script-title=ja:「ガチアクタ」7月6日放送開始、追加キャストに森川智之&新祐樹 本PVや主題歌情報も|url=https://natalie.mu/comic/news/626839|url-status=live|archive-url=https://megalodon.jp/2026-0305-0655-05/https://natalie.mu:443/comic/news/626839|archive-date=March 5, 2026|access-date=June 23, 2025|website=[[Music Natalie]]|publisher=Natasha, Inc|language=ja}}</ref> Prior to the television airing, the series received advanced screenings in more than 15 countries worldwide under the title ''Gachiakuta: World Takeover'', starting with the world premiere event at the {{Ill|Shinjuku Piccadilly|ja|新宿ピカデリー}} in [[Shinjuku]] on July 4 of the same year.<ref name="PremiereDate-ThemeSongs">{{Cite web|last=Hodgkins|first=Crystalyn|date=June 5, 2025|title=''Gachiakuta'' TV Anime Reveals Premiere Screenings in 15 Countries Before July 6 Debut|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-06-05/gachiakuta-tv-anime-reveals-premiere-screenings-in-15-countries-before-july-6-debut/.225193|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250606032914/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-06-05/gachiakuta-tv-anime-reveals-premiere-screenings-in-15-countries-before-july-6-debut/.225193|archive-date=June 6, 2025|access-date=June 6, 2025|website=[[Anime News Network]]}}</ref> For the first cours, the opening theme song is "Hugs", performed by {{Ill|Paledusk|ja}}, while the ending theme song is {{Nihongo|"Tomoshibi"|灯火}}, performed by {{Ill|Dustcell|ja|DUSTCELL}}.<ref name="PremiereDate-ThemeSongs"/> For the second cours, the opening theme song is "Let's Just Crash", performed by [[Mori Calliope]], while the ending theme song is {{Nihongo|"Ban"|番}}, performed by Karanoah.<ref name="2ndOP-ED-MoreCast">{{Cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|date=October 6, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-10-06/gachiakuta-anime-2nd-half-unveils-more-cast-theme-songs-in-video/.229690|title=''Gachiakuta'' Anime's 2nd Half Unveils More Cast, Theme Songs in Video|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251007024841/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-10-06/gachiakuta-anime-2nd-half-unveils-more-cast-theme-songs-in-video/.229690|archive-date=October 7, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=October 7, 2025}}</ref>

After the finale of the first season, a second season was announced.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Tai|first=Anita|date=December 21, 2025|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-12-21/gachiakuta-anime-gets-2nd-season/.232359|title=''Gachiakuta'' Anime Gets 2nd Season|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251221171611/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2025-12-21/gachiakuta-anime-gets-2nd-season/.232359|archive-date=December 21, 2025|url-status=live|access-date=December 21, 2025}}</ref>

[[Crunchyroll]] is streaming the series.<ref name="Cast"/> [[Medialink]] licensed the series in Southeast Asia for streaming on Ani-One Asia YouTube channel.<ref>{{Cite web|last=Pineda|first=Rafael Antonio|date=December 20, 2024|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-12-20/medialink-licenses-gachiakuta-anime-for-streaming-on-ani-one-in-2025/.219309|title=MediaLink Licenses ''Gachiakuta'' Anime for Streaming on Ani-One in 2025|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241226170831/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2024-12-20/medialink-licenses-gachiakuta-anime-for-streaming-on-ani-one-in-2025/.219309|archive-date=December 26, 2024|url-status=live|access-date=December 24, 2024}}</ref> The English dub for the series began broadcasting on [[Adult Swim]]'s [[Toonami]] programming block on October 18, 2026.<ref name="Toonami">{{Cite web|last=Mateo|first=Alex|date=October 2, 2026|url=https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-10-02/toonami-airs-wind-breaker-gachiakuta-anime/.242426|title=Toonami Airs ''Wind Breaker'', ''Gachiakuta'' Anime|website=[[Anime News Network]]|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20261002182819/https://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2026-10-02/toonami-airs-wind-breaker-gachiakuta-anime/.242426|archive-date=October 2, 2026|url-status=live|access-date=October 2, 2026|quote=Adult Swim's Toonami programming block revealed on Friday that it will air both the ''Wind Breaker'' and ''Gachiakuta'' anime in the United States starting on October 10 and 17, respectively (effectively, October 11 and 18).}}</ref>

