{{Cleanup|reason=Every volume summary starting with Volume 18 needs to be proofread for [[WP:TONE|tone]] and [[MOS:TENSE|tense]].|date=May 2018}}
[[File:Soul Eater manga volume 1.jpg|thumb|220px|The cover of the first volume of the ''[[Soul Eater (manga)|Soul Eater]]'' manga released by [[Gangan Comics]] on June 22, 2004, in Japan]]
''[[Soul Eater]]'' is a Japanese [[manga]] series written and illustrated by [[Atsushi Okubo]]. The series follows the adventures of three students at a school called the Death Weapon Meister Academy (or DWMA for short), known as meisters, who use demon weapon companions with human and weapon forms. These meisters, [[List of Soul Eater characters#Maka Albarn|Maka Albarn]], [[List of Soul Eater characters#Black Star|Black Star]], and [[List of Soul Eater characters#Death the Kid|Death the Kid]], seek to turn their weapons, [[List of Soul Eater characters#Soul Eater|Soul Eater]], [[List of Soul Eater characters#Tsubaki|Tsubaki]], and the [[List of Soul Eater characters#Liz and Patty Thompson|Thompson sisters]] respectively, into "death scythes" for [[List of Soul Eater characters#Death|Lord Death]], the [[Personifications of death|Grim Reaper]] and head of the DWMA, by having their weapons consume the souls of 99 evil humans and one witch.<ref name="story">{{cite web|url=http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/souleater/story_keyword/|title=Story section at manga's official website|access-date=April 20, 2008|language=Japanese|archive-date=December 18, 2011|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111218112419/http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/souleater/story_keyword/|url-status=dead}}</ref>

The manga initially began as three separate [[One-shot (comics)|one-shots]] serialized between June 24, 2003, and November 26, 2003, in two [[List of manga magazines|manga magazines]] published by [[Square Enix]]. The first one-shot was published in the summer 2003 special edition of ''[[Gangan Powered]]'',<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/powered/2003summer.html |title=Summer 2003 issue of ''Gangan Powered'' |publisher=[[Square Enix]] |access-date=April 20, 2008 |language=Japanese |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080502065544/http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/powered/2003summer.html |archive-date=May 2, 2008 |url-status=dead }}</ref> the second following in the autumn 2003 special edition of the same magazine,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/powered/2003autumn.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090202121900/http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/powered/2003autumn.html|title=Autumn 2003 issue of ''Gangan Powered''|publisher=[[Square Enix]]|archive-date=February 2, 2009|access-date=January 12, 2013|language=Japanese}}</ref> and the third serialized in ''[[Gangan Wing]]''. The manga started regular serialization in Square Enix's ''[[Monthly Shōnen Gangan]]'' magazine on May 12, 2004. The first {{Transliteration|ja|[[tankōbon]]}} was released by Square Enix under their ''[[Gangan Comics]]'' [[imprint (trade name)|imprint]] on June 22, 2004, in Japan; as of December 12, 2013, 25 volumes have been released.<ref name="manga-vol">{{cite web|url=http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/souleater/books/|title=Books section at manga's official website|publisher=[[Square Enix]]|access-date=February 21, 2010|language=Japanese|archive-date=March 23, 2012|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20120323135836/http://gangan.square-enix.co.jp/souleater/books/|url-status=dead}}</ref> The series is published in English by [[Yen Press]], and is serialized in Yen Press' ''Yen Plus'' manga anthology magazine. The first issue of ''Yen Plus'' was released on July 29, 2008.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2008-04-19/yen-announces-titles-to-run-in-anthology-magazine|title=Yen Press Announces Titles to Run in Anthology Mag|publisher=[[Anime News Network]]|date=April 19, 2008|access-date=April 19, 2008|archive-date=April 21, 2008|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080421002733/http://www.animenewsnetwork.com/news/2008-04-19/yen-announces-titles-to-run-in-anthology-magazine|url-status=live}}</ref>
